    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `complete_paragraph` in `app/tgi.py`, following the pattern in `app/titles.py`:\n\n```python\nclient = InferenceClient(model=endpoint_url)\ngenerated = client.text_generation(\n    prompt,\n    max_new_tokens=200,\n    stop=[\"\\n\\n\"],\n    return_full_text=False,\n)\nreturn generated.rstrip()\n```\n\n- **Stopping at a blank line:** I used `stop=[\"\\n\\n\"]`. In huggingface_hub 2.0.0, which this project pins, `text_generation()` no longer accepts `stop_sequences`. I confirmed `stop` is in the installed signature.\n- **Returning only the new text:** `return_full_text=False` leaves the prompt out of the result.\n- **Trailing whitespace:** TGI includes the matched stop sequence in its output, so `.rstrip()` removes that trailing `\"\\n\\n\"` along with any other trailing whitespace.\n\n`pytest -q` passes, but the only test checks that the module imports, so nothing has called a real TGI server. I didn't add any dependencies."
